.\" Version: 1.2
.\"
.TH saphanasr-rmhdbpid 8 "26 Aug 2026" "" "SAPHanaSR"
.\"
.SH NAME
.\"
saphanasr-rmhdbpid \- remove left-over HANA hdbdaemon PID file
.PP
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\"
\fBsaphanasr-rmhdbpid\fR [ --help | --version | --force ]
.PP
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\"
saphanasr-rmhdbpid can be used to remove HANA hdbdaemon PID files.
This might be useful, if a left-over PID file prevents HANA from starting right
after system boot.
.br
Do not call this script while HANA is running.
.PP
.\"
.SH OPTIONS
.\"
.TP 4
\fB --help\fR
show help.
.TP 4
\fB --version\fR
show version.
.TP 4
\fB --force\fR
force script execution.
.PP
.\"
.SH RETURN CODES
.\"
.B 0
Successful program execution.
.br
.B >0
Usage, syntax or execution errors.
.PP
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.\"
\fB*\fP enable and check systemd service saphanasr-rmhdbpid
.PP
.RS 2
# systemctl enable saphanasr-rmhdbpid
.br
# systemctl list-unit-files | grep -i saphanasr-rmhdbpid
.br
# systemctl status saphanasr-rmhdbpid
.br
# systemd-analyze dot | grep saphanasr-rmhdbpid
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fP show script messages
.PP
.RS 2
# grep saphanasr-rmhdbpid /var/log/messages
.RE
.PP
.\"
.SH FILES
.\"
.TP 4
/usr/share/SAPHanaSR-angi/bin/saphanasr-rmhdbpid
the script itself.
.TP 4
/usr/lib/systemd/system/saphanasr-rmhdbpid.service
the default unit file.
.TP 4
/usr/sap/<SID>/HDB<INO>/<HOST>/lock/hdbdaemon@3<INO>00.pid
the hdbdaemon PID file.
.PP
.\"
.SH BUGS
.\"
In case of any problem, please use your favourite SAP support process to open a
request for the component BC-OP-LNX-SUSE.
.\" TODO Please report any other feedback and suggestions to feedback@suse.com.
.PP
.\"
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.\"
\fB*\fP This script is needed only, when left-over hdbdaemon PID files sporadically
prevent HANA from starting.
.PP
\fB*\fP This script should run as systemd service at boot time.
It must not be called while HANA is running.
.PP
\fB*\fP The systemd service saphanasr-rmhdbpid needs to be enabled.
.PP
\fB*\fP The directory /usr/sap/<SID>/HDB<INO>/<HOST>/lock/ needs to be accessible
at boot time. 
.PP
.\"
.SH SEE ALSO
.\"
\fBsystemctl\fP(8)
.PP
